a2:CHEBI_32159 owl:sameAs a2:CHEBI_32159 ;
    rdfs:subClassOf a2:FOODON_03412972 , a2:CHEBI_36683 ;
    rdfs:label "sucralose" ;
    rdfs:comment """LanguaL term definition: Food additive; technological purpose(s): sweetener.


Sucralose is an artificial sweetener. The majority of ingested sucralose is not broken down by the body and therefore it is non-caloric. In the European Union, it is also known under the E number (additive code) E955. Sucralose is approximately 600 times as sweet as sucrose (table sugar), twice as sweet as saccharin, and 3 times as sweet as aspartame.""" , 'LanguaL curation note: See "food additive" comments.' ;
    rdf:type owl:Class .

