a2:FOODON_03311834 owl:sameAs a2:FOODON_03311834 ;
    rdfs:subClassOf owl:Thing ;
    rdfs:label "virginia peanut pod (raw)" , "ballpark peanut" ;
    rdfs:comment "The large-seeded Virginia group peanuts are grown in the US states of Virginia, North Carolina, Tennessee, Texas, New Mexico, Oklahoma, and parts of Georgia. They are increasing in popularity due to demand for large peanuts for processing, particularly for salting, confections, and roasting in the shells. [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Peanut#Virginia_group]. Virginia peanuts account for about 15 percent of total U. S. production. [https://www.nationalpeanutboard.org/peanut-info/peanut-types.htm]" , """SIREN DB annotation:
* has quality 'whole, natural shape' (http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03430150)
* has quality 'not heat-treated' (http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03440003)
* derives from 'seed (anatomical part)' (http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03420155)
        """ ;
    rdf:type owl:Class .

"The large-seeded Virginia group peanuts are grown in the US states of Virginia, North Carolina, Tennessee, Texas, New Mexico, Oklahoma, and parts of Georgia. They are increasing in popularity due to demand for large peanuts for processing, particularly for salting, confections, and roasting in the shells. [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Peanut#Virginia_group]. Virginia peanuts account for about 15 percent of total U. S. production. [https://www.nationalpeanutboard.org/peanut-info/peanut-types.htm]" owl:sameAs "The large-seeded Virginia group peanuts are grown in the US states of Virginia, North Carolina, Tennessee, Texas, New Mexico, Oklahoma, and parts of Georgia. They are increasing in popularity due to demand for large peanuts for processing, particularly for salting, confections, and roasting in the shells. [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Peanut#Virginia_group]. Virginia peanuts account for about 15 percent of total U. S. production. [https://www.nationalpeanutboard.org/peanut-info/peanut-types.htm]" .

"ballpark peanut" owl:sameAs "ballpark peanut" .

"virginia peanut pod (raw)" owl:sameAs "virginia peanut pod (raw)" .

