a2:FOODON_03440018 owl:sameAs a2:FOODON_03440018 ;
    rdfs:subClassOf a2:FOODON_03440022 ;
    rdfs:label "partially heat-treated" ;
    rdfs:comment "LanguaL curation note: Used when heat was applied to a food product for a time sufficient to partially change its flavor and textural characteristics and to cause some chemical changes and/or some reduction in enzyme and microbial activity. The product can be readied for consumption in a shortened cooking time. Products labeled 'quick cooking' are often partially heat treated. Some products are consumed partially heat-treated, e.g., pasteurized milk, blanched broccoli, or rare beef." ;
    rdf:type owl:Class .

